# Keep the base pipeline pristine and remove `game/mods` from supported input

The canonical port pipeline builds only the faithful base game. `game/mods/`
must stop being an officially supported pipeline input; legacy mod packages are
handled later by separate user-facing conversion/import tooling.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Remove `game/mods/`, `m.lmlm`, `j.lmlm`, and any optional-mod approval
  path from the canonical base extraction/conversion/build pipeline.
- [x] Preserve existing files while migrating/removing pipeline behavior; never
  silently delete user-owned mod packages.
- [x] Keep Jebano and Muckluck packages only as explicit converter test fixtures
  or local test inputs, never automatic content injected into the base game.
- [x] Ensure a normal base build is byte/provenance independent of whether any
  local mod package exists elsewhere on the machine.
- [x] Update README mod/install language when implementation lands so it never
  tells users to place legacy mods in the source-game pipeline.

## Dependencies

No dependency: this is a P0 product-authority correction.

## Evidence

The canonical base-source extraction no longer exposes `export-lmlm`,
optional-mod preview, or approval-token paths, and its complete extraction is
nine
faithful-base stages. Phase-two metadata/index routing contains no LMLM override
categories,
and the game-manifest taxonomy contains no `language_mod` kind or synthetic
`.lmlm` requirement. The scanner gives `.lmlm` no special exemption, so legacy
packages inside a claimed base source are unclassified rather than supported.
A separate repository-root `mods/` user-input boundary may be composed after the
base extraction; it is not evidence for validating `game/`.

Legacy compatibility now lives only in the separately downloadable,
Rust-only `tools/lmlm/` compatibility boundary (Rust 1.97.1). Its read-only
inspector validated the local Jebano and Muckluck inputs without installing or
extracting
them. No user-owned package was moved or deleted by the repository migration.

Validation evidence: `cargo test -p game_manifest` passed; the full pipeline
library suite passed after removal; the retired CLI commands have an explicit
unknown-command contract test; `tools/lmlm` has passing Rust parser/converter
tests; and
the canonical local `game/` passes `validate-game` with 109 base folder/type
minimums plus exact root-file requirements. Source traversal remains rooted in
the caller-selected game directory, so packages elsewhere on the machine are
not base-build evidence.
